\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S2}{\ignorespaces Operational specification of the retrieval loop and of every allocation rule. All rules share the loop, the batch size, the probe, the tie-breaking and the stopping test; they differ only in the score $\sigma _j$ and in which point value $\tilde  \theta _j$ of the posterior they use. $R_j$: reads spent on container $j$; $U_j$: fragments of container $j$ verified from its own reads; $n_j$: fragments stored in $j$; $h_{ij}$: hazard that unrecovered fragment $i$ in $j$ becomes decodable within the next batch; $\mathcal  O$: fragments of stripes that still need fragments.}}{2}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:algorithms}{{S2}{2}{}{}{}}
